<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Adaptive icon background layer — deliberately fully transparent.

  Do not "fix" this by painting the brand gradient here: that is what makes the icon come out as
  the launcher's shape instead of ours.

  On Android the launcher, not the app, decides an adaptive icon's silhouette — it masks both
  layers to its own shape (a circle on plenty of launchers, a squircle on Pixel-family ones). An
  opaque background therefore fills that mask edge to edge and the icon simply *becomes* a circle
  wherever the mask is one.

  A mask only ever crops, so the way to keep our own squircle is to stay inside it: the foreground
  holds the complete squircle artwork sized so its corners sit within the mask's inscribed circle
  (measured corner reach is 1.21x that circle's radius; see ic_launcher_foreground), and everything
  around it is transparent. No mask then touches a single pixel of the icon, and the shape is the
  same squircle on every launcher.

  A vector rather than a colour drawable so the layer reports real 108dp bounds — see git history
  for the launchers whose icon-caching paths size their render target from intrinsic bounds.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <path
        android:pathData="M0,0h108v108h-108z"
        android:fillColor="#00000000" />
</vector>
